        "original_id": "782e585a-f18f-53d6-82d1-ac81554b7fdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Panicum, Populus, Echinochloa colona\n- Fungi: Exserohilum echinochloae\n- Places: Tropical regions, Northern Hemisphere, Bangladesh\n- Concepts: Taxonomy, native range, species classification\n\nFacts:\n- Panicum is a large genus of about 450 grass species native throughout the tropical regions of the world, with a few species extending into the northern temperate zone.\n- Populus is a genus of 25–35 deciduous flowering plant species in the family Salicaceae native to most of the Northern Hemisphere.\n- Echinochloa colona was formerly classified as a species of Panicum.\n- Exserohilum echinochloae was described as new to science in 1984.\n- Exserohilum echinochloae is found in Bangladesh, where it grows on the leaves of Echinochloa colona.",
